      "title": "Epistemic vs deontic modal readings",
      "objective": "Disambiguate probability, obligation, permission and volition from context.",
      "concept": {
        "en": "Interpret modal verbs by context because the same modal can express probability, obligation, permission or volition.",
        "vi": "Giải thích động từ khuyết thiếu dựa vào ngữ cảnh vì cùng một modal có thể biểu thị suy đoán, nghĩa vụ, sự cho phép hoặc ý chí."
      },
      "formulae": [
        "modal + base verb",
        "modal + be/have + complement"
      ],
      "whenToUse": [
        "Resolve meaning when a modal form has more than one possible semantic reading.",
        "Choose surrounding context that makes epistemic and deontic meanings clear."
      ],
      "forms": {
        "positive": [
          "They must be asleep. (deduction)",
          "Visitors must wear a badge. (obligation)",
          "You may use this room. (permission)"
        ]
      },
      "variations": [
        "Prosody, subject choice, lexical aspect and surrounding discourse can remove or create ambiguity."
