      "title": "Marked word order for rhetorical effect",
      "objective": "Use fronting, inversion and end-focus intentionally rather than accidentally.",
      "concept": {
        "en": "Marked word order moves information away from the neutral pattern to create focus, scene-setting or rhetorical rhythm.",
        "vi": "Trật tự từ đánh dấu cố ý thay đổi trật tự trung tính để tạo điểm nhấn, dựng bối cảnh hoặc tạo nhịp điệu tu từ."
      },
      "formulae": [
        "Fronted locative + verb + subject (with suitable verbs).",
        "Fronted complement + linking verb + subject in selected formal styles."
      ],
      "whenToUse": [
        "Literary/descriptive scene-setting.",
        "Formal rhetoric where the marked order improves information flow rather than merely sounding unusual."
      ],
      "forms": {
